<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phoenicians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Phoenician</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Phoenicians were a Semitic-speaking seafaring people of the Levantine coast, based in city-states such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidon">Sidon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a>. From the ninth century BCE they founded trading posts across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, which grew into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>. Phoenician trade in luxury goods also supplied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>, which dominated the Phoenician cities.</p></div>
